Backward compatibility is ensured by allowing Shopify product catalogs to be imported via CSV. A critical requirement is that historical order data must be migrated without any loss. During the transition period, both the old and new systems will run in parallel to facilitate a smooth handover.

Specific latency and throughput targets have been established. The p95 latency for loading a product list must be less than 200ms, even with up to 100,000 products. End-to-end order placement should complete in under 3 seconds. Search queries against a 100,000-item catalog must return results in less than 200ms, and individual inventory lookups are targeted to complete in under 50ms per SKU.

